
# AIDA distributed store (orphan branch worktree)
# Bare-name pattern catches session-worktree symlinks back to the
# canonical store. trace:EPIC-21 | ai:claude
.aida-store/
.aida-store

# AIDA runtime state — deny-by-default. Anything under .aida/ is
# per-clone runtime state (cache, sessions, roles, env shims, review
# prompts, server data, etc.) unless explicitly allow-listed below.
# Adding a new runtime file under .aida/ requires no gitignore change;
# tracking a new project-config file requires an explicit `!` line.
# trace:BUG-73 | ai:claude
.aida/*

# Tracked exceptions: project-level config that lives in the repo.
!.aida/config.toml
# Project-level command aliases are shareable across the team.
# trace:TASK-877 | ai:claude
!.aida/aliases.toml

# Per-project skill extensions are tracked project assets, not
# runtime state — they live under .claude/ which is tracked by
# default. Do not add ignore rules for .claude/skills/local/ or
# any <skill>.local.md file; the whole team should pick them up on
# `git pull`. See docs/extending-skills.md. trace:STORY-305 | ai:claude

# The AIDA project manifest is checked in: it describes what this
# project IS (description, why it exists, liveness, stage, owner) and
# is meant to travel with the repository. trace:STORY-781 | ai:claude
!.aida/project.toml

# AIDA-using discipline guides are checked in with the project.
# trace:STORY-829 | ai:codex
!.aida/discipline/
!.aida/discipline/**

# Personal Claude Code notes — per-machine, never team-shared.
# CLAUDE.local.md loads alongside CLAUDE.md at session start but
# stays out of git so reviewer-feedback dumps + personal-habit
# reminders stay private. See the scaffolded file's own header
# for usage guidance.
CLAUDE.local.md

# AIDA path-gated rules generated by `aida rules sync` — per-clone
# derived state. Hand-authored rules outside this subdir stay
# tracked. trace:SPIKE-31 | ai:claude
.claude/rules/aida-specs/

# AIDA planning-pass drafts — scratch plans; promote to
# docs/plans/<name>.md when adopted. Gitignored so they don't conflict
# with a later PR's landed plan. trace:TASK-383 | ai:claude
docs/plans/_draft/

# Per-user Claude Code overrides — never team-shared.
# .claude/settings.local.json holds local MCP trust (the aida server
# pre-approval) and personal settings. Gitignored so a committed
# pre-approval can't become a clone-attack vector. trace:BUG-484
.claude/settings.local.json

# Rust build artifacts
target/

